{{Quote|This humane device attaches to its target and dispenses repeated electrical pulses, keeping the target in place for humane apprehension and/or termination.|[[Armory]] Description}}

The '''G-109 Urchin''' is a [[Weapons#Special-2|Special Throwable]] that can stick and inflict stun to a single target after a delay. 

== Procurement ==
The {{PAGENAME}} is unlocked on the 3rd page of the [[Force of Law Premium Warbond]] for {{Currency|Medals|65}}.

== Detailed Weapon Statistics ==
{{Attack_Data Weapon}}

== Tactical Information ==
* The Urchin can be imagined like a cross between the [[G-23 Stun]] and the [[G-123 Thermite]] grenade. Rather than explode and deal damage, it sticks to enemies and periodically emits a pulse in a small area.
** After being thrown, it emits one pulse every 2.9s for a total of 4 pulses.
* The small explosion radius on the grenade is compensated by its long stun effect, lasting about 13.7 seconds in total from the first pulse, and a high stagger force capable of staggering even [[Bile Titan|Bile Titans]].
** Helldivers can take advantage of this by exploiting an enemy's weak spots or using offensive [[Stratagems]].
** Despite the small explosion radius, it is still possible to stun multiple enemies in tight corners.
* As this grenade has 0 demolition force, it cannot destroy structures such as [[Bug Hole|Bug Holes]] or [[Automaton Fabricator|Automaton Fabricators]].
* Unlike other grenades, the Urchin's fuse time begins after the grenade is thrown.
** This gives Helldivers enough time to aim at the enemy without the risk of detonating the grenade in their hands.
* If Helldivers are caught in the range of an Urchin Grenade's blast, their stamina will be immediately depleted. The [[SH-32 Shield Generator Pack]] can negate this effect for as long as it is active, but actions such as using a terminal or stimming will be interrupted.
* Much like the [[K-2 Throwing Knife]], the Urchin is one of the few throwables that won't alert enemies if it enters their detection radius. 
** Enemies affected by this also won't detect the Helldiver who threw it, and will simply return to their original position.
** To aid its playstyle, it also makes no noise when pulsing, keeping Helldivers undetected from enemies.

