{{Quote|Creates a far-reaching incendiary blast ideal for crowd control against smaller enemies of Freedom. Equipped with a programmable timer for strategic versatility.|Armory Description}}

The '''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Weapons#Throwable-0|Standard Throwable]] with a wide and high damaging explosion, at the cost of a longer than usual fuse. Uniquely, it has a programmable fuse timer which can be changed via the weapon wheel.

== Procurement ==
The {{PAGENAME}} is unlocked on the 3rd page of the [[Borderline Justice Premium Warbond]] for {{Currency|Medals|65}}.

== Detailed Weapon Statistics ==
{{Attack_Data_Weapon|TED-63 DYNAMITE}}

== Tactical Information ==
* The Dynamite can be considered an upgrade to the [[G-12 High Explosive]]. It deals 25% more damage, has a larger inner and outer radius, and more demolition force (40 vs 30). The only drawbacks would be 1 fewer grenade and a longer fuse.
* This grenade can destroy [[Bug Hole]]s, [[Bile Titan Bug Hole]]s, and [[Automaton Fabricator]]s without needing to be thrown into them, thanks to its demolition 40 explosion.
** [[Bulk Fabricator]]s and [[Grounded Warp Ship]]s, however, need the grenade to be thrown into them.
** Certain configurations of [[Bug Nest]]s can be destroyed with a single Dynamite, due to the large radius and the aforementioned high demo force.
* The programmable fuse timer can be configured to have a 5, 15, or 60-second duration. Longer timers are harder to deal precise damage with, but can aid in taking out patrols and static spawns with its large area of effect undetected, as the Helldiver can put a larger distance between them and the dynamite before the sound can alert enemies to their location.
** The 60-second timer can be used to great effect in stealthily clearing outposts or other destruction objectives on [https://helldivers.wiki.gg/wiki/Stealth#Commando_Missions Commando Missions]. When paired with a [[B-1 Supply Pack]], it can be used as an alternative to the [[B/MD C4 Pack]].
*** Compared to the [[B/MD C4 Pack]], this combo has higher "capacity" (4 dynamites + 8 from resupplies vs 6 C4 charges), but less armor penetration ({{Armor|4|AP}} vs {{Armor|7|AP}}) and less damage (1,000 vs 2,000). However, the Dynamite + Supply Pack combo leaves the support weapon slot cleared, while the C4 pack does not. Lastly, the C4 pack allows for on-command detonations instead of a timer.

