{{Quote|A throwable anti-personnel mine, capable of adhering to most surfaces. Upon deployment, emits lights and sounds which attract nearby hostiles to its proximity-activated detonator.|Armory Description}}

The '''{{PAGENAME}}''' is a [[Weapons#Special-2|Special Throwable]] that lures in enemies before proximity detonating with a high damage explosion and shrapnel.

== Procurement ==
The {{PAGENAME}} is unlocked on the 3rd page of the [[Redacted Regiment Premium Warbond]] for {{Currency|Medals|65}} 

== Detailed Weapon Statistics ==
{{Attack_Data_Weapon|TM-1 Lure Mine}}

== Tactical Information ==
* The Lure Mine does not have a standard fuse - it will remain where it is thrown instead, attracting enemies until they get close enough for it to explode. It is armed immediately upon sticking to a surface.
* The Lure Mine has a significantly shorter throwing range than other throwables, only being able to be thrown a few meters away. It is highly recommended to aim upwards when throwing to ensure Helldivers don't die when it lands and arms.
** Alternatively, Helldivers may utilise the [[Desert Stormer]] or [[Servo-Assisted]] armor passives to increase the throwing range.
* One of the best attributes of the Lure Mine is its ability to distract enemies even if they're already attacking Helldivers by tossing the mine away from their position, creating opportunities to reposition, retreat, or counterattack more effectively.
* An effective strategy using the Lure Mine is to place it on or next to a [[Damaged Hellbomb]], inside of an allied minefield, or a [[A/ARC-3 Tesla Tower]], potentially drawing entire patrols to their doom. 
* The Lure Mine can destroy [[Bug Hole]]s, [[Automaton Fabricator]]s and [[Bulk Fabricator]]s, but its unpractical to use due their non-standard fuse. There are two ways to explode the mine:
** By shooting at it.
** By throwing it next to where enemies will appear. Note that [[Bug Hole]]s can be destroyed only if the mine is thrown inside the hole.

